rt and money toward  fundraising efforts to find a cure for  the metabolic disease among the  organizations Cate supports is the  Juvenile Diabetes Research Foundation  which puts on benefits like rock The  Cure and the promise ball to raise money  for research a new calling  Kate's lives in Manhattan's fancy Upper  East Side which is also where she  operates an upscale boutique called blue  tree the store started off selling  expensive designer toys but is expanded  to include clothing housewares and  specialty foods  she told the USA Today in 2006  I always wanted to have a general store  if I could have a photobooth Ansel's  candy I would have clearly cases opens  the idea of selling all kinds of things  at blue tree so would she sell a mocha  why then I'll give you $200 that's $200  I'm sorry  mo why not for sale oh well probably  better off thanks for watching subscribe  to our YouTube channel to watch more  videos like the one you just saw and  leave us a comment to let us know which  other 80 stars you'd love to see make a  comeback  [Music]
 

